ggml-headers-source: whisper-rs-sys 0.15.0, whisper.cpp/ggml/include
ggml-headers-whisper-cpp-version: 1.8.3

build.rs refuses to build when whisper-rs-sys reports a different whisper.cpp version
(DEP_WHISPER_WHISPER_CPP_VERSION) than ggml-headers-whisper-cpp-version.

local changes in whisper-diarization.cpp:
  1. gguf_get_tensor_ne does not exist in ggml 1.8.3. whisper_diar_model_load asks
     gguf_init_from_file for a no_alloc ggml context of the file's tensors (file_ctx)
     and reads each tensor's shape from it with ggml_get_tensor(file_ctx, name)->ne.
     The shape check against the expected tensor stays as upstream.
  2. whisper_diar_log_callback_default forwards every line to the callback installed
     with speedwave_diar_log_set (new extern "C" function) and prints nothing without
     one, so the log reaches the Rust log facade instead of stderr.
  3. #include "whisper-diarization.h" instead of #include "whisper.h".
  4. speedwave_diar_abi_sizes (new extern "C" function) reports the sizes of
     whisper_diar_context_params and whisper_diar_params, so a Rust test can compare
     them with its #[repr(C)] mirrors.
  5. whisper_diar_model_load opens the model for reading with a UTF-16 path under
     MSVC, as whisper.cpp 1.8.3 does in whisper_init_from_file_with_params_no_state;
     a narrow std::ifstream path is read in the ANSI code page there and fails for a
     data directory with non-ASCII characters. gguf_init_from_file already handles
     UTF-8 through ggml_fopen.
  6. whisper_diar_cache_params carries the geometry of NeMo-Speech.cpp's v3-offline
     preset (DiarGeometry::v3_offline in src/asr/diar/aosc_state.h: speaker cache 264,
     FIFO 0, chunk 264, cache update period 188, left and right context 1) instead of
     the low-latency streaming one (264, 80, 13, 40, no left context). The chunk loop
     in whisper_diar_detect_speakers, whisper_diar_process and whisper_diar_cache_update
     take a left context: its frames enter the graph but neither the output
     probabilities nor the FIFO, as in NeMo-Speech.cpp's AoscState::update.
